module

public import Mathlib.NumberTheory.Padics.PadicNumbers
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.AlgebraicClosure
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Algebraic.Defs
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IntermediateField.Adjoin.Defs
import Mathlib.FieldTheory.Separable
import Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Field.Krasner
import Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Field.Approximation
import Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Unbundled.SpectralNorm
import WeilConjectures.NumberTheory.Padics.Extension

/-! # Rational-algebraic simple overfields of p-adic algebraic elements

Source: Stanford Weil II seminar, L19, Proposition 1.1.9, first bullet, p. 3;
`WeilConjectures/NumberTheory/Padics/Extension.lean`,
`PadicAlgCl.exists_isAlgebraic_mem_adjoin_simple`
(blueprint: lem-sfb-padic-rational-algebraic-generator).

The statement allows an arbitrary algebraic closure in any universe. The rational
algebra structure is the composite of the canonical map into the p-adic numbers
with the specified p-adic algebra structure; no extra characteristic hypothesis is needed.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace Padic

/-- Every element of an algebraic closure of the p-adic numbers lies in a simple
extension generated by an element algebraic over the rationals.

Source: Stanford Weil II seminar, L19, Proposition 1.1.9, first bullet, p. 3;
`PadicAlgCl.exists_isAlgebraic_mem_adjoin_simple` in the project's p-adic Extension module
(blueprint: lem-sfb-padic-rational-algebraic-generator).

Proof:
1. The p-adic base is complete, nonarchimedean, nontrivially normed, of characteristic zero,
   and contains the rationals densely (def-weil-l-adic-numbers). Since the closure is
   algebraic (def-weil-algebraic-closure), lem-trf-spectral-norm-algebraic-extension equips
   it with a multiplicative nonarchimedean norm extending that of the base.
2. For the given x, take its monic irreducible minimal polynomial f, of positive degree n
   (def-weil-pbc-separable-algebraic-extension). Characteristic zero makes its derivative
   nonzero, so lem-trf-irreducible-separable-derivative gives separability. By
   lem-pc-separable-polynomial-distinct-roots-alg-closed, f splits with n distinct roots.
3. Let S be the finite set of roots other than x. If S is empty take delta = 1; otherwise
   take delta to be the minimum of the positive distances from x to members of S.
   Then delta is positive and bounds every other conjugate distance from below.
4. Put M = max(norm x, 1) and epsilon = (delta / M)^n / (n + 1). Apply
   lem-sfb-monic-dense-approximation to approximate f by a monic rational polynomial g
   of degree n with each coefficient error less than epsilon. Its image h over the
   p-adic base remains monic of degree n.
5. The polynomial h splits in the closure: successively remove linear factors using
   def-weil-algebraic-closure, with the monic degree-zero polynomial as the base case.
   By lem-sfb-roots-coefficient-proximity it has a root b with
   norm(x - b) < ((n + 1) * epsilon)^(1/n) * M = delta.
6. Evaluation of g and h at b agrees because their coefficient maps agree through the
   prime field. Since g is nonzero and g(b) = 0, def-weil-algebraic-element gives that
   b is algebraic over the rationals.
7. For each other conjugate y, norm(x - b) < delta <= norm(x - y).
   The separability, splitting and norm-extension hypotheses having been checked,
   lem-sfb-complete-normed-krasner yields x in the p-adic field generated by b.
-/
theorem exists_isAlgebraic_rat_mem_adjoin_simple_of_isAlgClosure
    (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime] (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω]
    [Algebra (Padic l) Ω] [IsAlgClosure (Padic l) Ω] (x : Ω) :
    ∃ b : Ω,
      @IsAlgebraic ℚ Ω _ _
        ((algebraMap (Padic l) Ω).comp (algebraMap ℚ (Padic l))).toAlgebra b ∧
      x ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin (Padic l) ({b} : Set Ω) := by
  sorry

end Padic
